			<h3>Keys</h3>
			<p id="keysName" class="muted"></p>
			<p class="hint">Any key opens the vault. Adding, changing, or removing a key is instant and never re-encrypts your files. Each action below asks for the password it needs the moment you choose it — nothing is typed here ahead of time. A recovery key protects you if you forget your password.</p>
			<div id="keysList" class="keys-list"></div>
			<p class="hint">A keyfile is any file — for example one kept on a USB stick — that unlocks the vault on its own. The file is fingerprinted in your browser and never leaves your machine; only its name is remembered as a hint.</p>
			<input type="file" id="keysKeyfile" hidden>
			<div id="keysResult" class="tamper-result" hidden></div>
